e GE vendor the one  that costs nine hundred GE credits has  been removed instead this vendor will  now sell individual caches  her classified gear said for each global  event so for example if striker is  available in the current global event  there will be a strike a cache available  for purchase there guarantees an item  from the striker set removed premium  vendor exotics from the open world loop  pool and exotic caches all exotics added  to the open world bosses this should  mean that farming for exotics gets a  little bit easier  no more will ever getting multiple  cassadee's per week just a quick tip if  you're not already doing it hold on to  your exotic caches until the update  drops and then open them up when their  changes have been implemented for a  better chance of getting what you  actually want classified drop rates have  been increased in all locations the  legendary missions now have a 20% chance  to give classified gear as a reward at  the completion of the mission season  pass supply drops now have a temp same  chance to drop classified gear survival  caches now has a roughly 10% chance to  drop classified gear it's not going to  be raining classifieds or anything but  the existing ways of getting classified  gear has basically had their drop rates  doubled in most cases and with the  addition of legendary missions and  survival caches now dropping them we're  certainly going to be seeing them a lot  more often they're doing this to help  close that gap between the hardcore  players already have everything and the  more casual and new players as per usual  there's a bunch of bug fixes that have  been included in this update I won't go  over all of them  most are quite specific and win exactly  game breaking I'll leave a link to the  full one point 8.1 patch notes in the  description but the following are  probably the most important bug fixes to  take note of  [Music]  this video will be more of a reminder to  a lot of you but I know there is a  